{"id":"chatentry-kind-union","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"ChatEntry becomes a union discriminated on kind #deferral","doing":true,"desc":"- ChatEntry is a flat struct with a dozen kind-specific optional fields, while its own docstring claims 'a union of six kinds' — so consumers (running.ts, statusOf) must re-establish facts the type should carry (status means nothing on a non-call row; a server-defaulted field re-defaulted client-side).\n- Discriminating the wire type on kind touches the transcript writer, every consumer's narrowing, and the wire contract — a design the human must rule, not a fold-in (#324's author argued it; grok's review concurred: a standing shape, not a cleanup that work parked).","created":"2026-08-21T17:18:39-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T17:26:56-04:00","custom":{"from":"#324","ruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~17:3x (question tool) — TYPE-ONLY: the union is compile-time over the unchanged encoding (wire and stored bytes identical, no migration); and the consumers' now-redundant defensive re-checks are DELETED in the same PR"}}
{"id":"filter-ask-carries-revision","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a1","title":"A filtered page re-searches the whole vault every frame #needs-brainstorm #deferral","doing":true,"desc":"- Measured in #290 on a 90k-node vault: one bulk gesture costs nine whole-vault search calls, one per frame. No client-side coalescing window can honestly reduce it (built both ways, measured 9→8, deleted).\n- The fix is on the server side: either the ask carries the page's revision so an unmoved set is answered from what was already computed, or the narrowing moves to the server with the reading.\n- Wants a short design note first: which of the two, the wire shape, and what the reconnect re-ask becomes.","see":["reactivity-kolu-upstream"],"created":"2026-08-20T14:01:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T14:57:42-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #290 deferral"}}
